  "label": "Stereotype of 'brown girl' as studious or academically inclined",
  "description": "The term 'brown girl' in the text overlay is a racialized descriptor that, in contemporary usage, often carries implicit associations with resilience, academic excellence, or cultural representation. While not inherently derogatory in this context, it relies on real-world social perceptions and media portrayals that have historically framed people of color — particularly young women — as either hyper-intelligent or as embodying 'model minority' tropes. The meme uses this term to evoke a relatable, positive image, but the term itself is rooted in broader societal categorizations and cultural narratives that are not visible in the image.",
